## Team Communication & Policies

- **Practice and game attendance is mandatory.** If an athlete is unable to attend, I must receive an email notification from a parent or guardian as soon as possible, and well in advance of the absence. Please make sure to cc attendance ({{attendance_email}}) as well.
- **You must bring your own water bottle.** Beaver does not provide team water and we do not allow sharing to prevent the spread of disease.
- Practice ends at 3:35pm and buses depart at 3:45. **If you take the bus, please bring your backpack to the practice location.**
- There will be some games when we will return to campus after the late bus at 5:45, thus students will miss the bus on these days. Please make transportation arrangements on these dates.
- **Uniforms are your responsibility!** You will be issued a uniform at the start of the season and you are responsible for laundering it and bringing it to school for games. We have a limited number of extras and so, in the event that you do forget your uniform please notify a coach before noon on game day.

## Playing Time

At the MS level we will do our best to get every player into every contest, although playing time may not be equal during every game/match.

As part of our policy, we do not discuss playing time with parents before, during, or immediately after games. If you'd like to discuss playing time with me, please abide by the "24 hour" rule and contact me 24 hours after a game or match.

## Coaching from the Sidelines

Please, do not coach from the sideline. Coaching is defined as giving direction, advice or suggestions on what to do on the field or court, during the game/match or during breaks of a game/match.

Things like: "shoot," "pass," "send it," "press," "kick it," and "throw it" are all examples of "coaching." Kids need to learn how to react and make decisions on their own, and it's OK if they make a mistake. Coaches should be the only ones coaching; it is too confusing for kids to try to listen to you, us and their teammates - it really does not help.

Please cheer loud and positively for our team, and encourage our athletes!

